WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.803
An authenticated request is not automatically permitted to change a system.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.914
The app session answers who may invoke the application.

00:00:06.914 --> 00:00:11.408
The change-intent control answers whether this read-only workshop may perform the
requested action.

00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:15.210
The recorded change test returns approval required with zero model calls.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.284
That is the expected safety outcome.

00:00:17.284 --> 00:00:23.161
The server stops before inference rather than asking the model to decide whether the
user has permission.

00:00:23.161 --> 00:00:27.309
It also avoids spending quota on a request that cannot be executed.

00:00:27.309 --> 00:00:31.803
A useful demonstration pairs the app outcome with the actual guard in code.

00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:34.569
A badge that says secure is not evidence.

00:00:34.569 --> 00:00:39.408
The meaningful question is which condition runs, in what order, and what it
prevents.

00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:42.302
The early change stop is one guardrail.

00:00:42.302 --> 00:00:49.342
Others validate the request shape, the selected service, each tool argument, maximum
calls, output size, quota, and error handling.

00:00:49.342 --> 00:00:54.529
A prompt-injection attempt can arrive in a ticket description, a runbook or tool
output.

00:00:54.529 --> 00:00:57.864
Those fields are data, not a new instruction hierarchy.

00:00:57.864 --> 00:01:02.681
Explain that boundary in the prompt, but enforce what you can in code.

00:01:02.681 --> 00:01:08.239
A ticket cannot add a shell tool if the registry contains only two read-only
fixtures.

00:01:08.239 --> 00:01:12.685
A model cannot query another service if argument validation rejects the mismatch.

00:01:12.685 --> 00:01:18.984
A tool exception should end or fail the bounded operation honestly, not cause a
silent unrestricted retry.

00:01:18.984 --> 00:01:21.578
No single test proves universal injection resistance.

00:01:21.578 --> 00:01:25.283
We demonstrate specific controls and keep their practical limits visible.

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:28.551
The ordinary user sees an answer or failure.

00:01:28.551 --> 00:01:31.891
The operator needs to understand the operation behind it.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.746
How many model calls occurred?

00:01:33.746 --> 00:01:34.859
Which tools ran?

00:01:34.859 --> 00:01:37.827
Did the policy stop the request before inference?

00:01:37.827 --> 00:01:40.053
How long did the calls take?

00:01:40.053 --> 00:01:43.392
Did export fail, and at which safe diagnostic stage?

00:01:43.392 --> 00:01:48.215
OpenTelemetry gives us a structured way to represent operations as traces and spans.

00:01:48.215 --> 00:01:50.070
A trace groups one run.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.667
A span describes one part of it.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:02:01.200
Parent and child relationships help us connect the application request,
authorization, generations and tools without pretending that every event is an
independent application.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.684
This is observable execution.

00:02:02.684 --> 00:02:08.992
It is not a request to expose hidden chain-of-thought, full account identity, or
every prompt and answer.

00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:17.695
For the simple Langfuse connection, the user supplies a base URL, a project public
key and a project secret key through protected server secrets.

00:02:17.695 --> 00:02:22.597
The variable names are LANGFUSE BASE URL, LANGFUSE PUBLIC KEY and LANGFUSE SECRET
KEY.

00:02:22.597 --> 00:02:27.498
Never paste their values into builder chat, a public repository or a browser
variable.

00:02:27.498 --> 00:02:30.649
The three values alone do not instrument an app.

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:37.652
The server must create and finish the right spans, serialize a valid payload and
export it to the validated destination.

00:02:37.652 --> 00:02:42.904
The app also needs a safe missing-configuration state and a way to show export
status.

00:02:42.904 --> 00:02:47.105
The course provides an implementation prompt and source reference for this work.

00:02:47.105 --> 00:02:55.158
Each builder should use its own clearly named Langfuse project and corresponding
server binding, so the evidence remains attributable to the intended app.

00:02:55.458 --> 00:03:01.238
The reference exporter uses an isolated telemetry provider rather than registering a
global auto-instrumentation pipeline.

00:03:01.238 --> 00:03:03.550
It records a bounded span batch.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:13.569
It allowlists metadata attributes, projects names to fixed known values, removes
span events and links, and drops default resource information that is unnecessary
for the lesson.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:15.881
The exported service name is generic.

00:03:15.881 --> 00:03:20.505
Prompt text, answer text, account identity and raw tool payloads are absent.

00:03:20.505 --> 00:03:27.827
Even metadata can be sensitive, so allowlisting is a design choice, not a guarantee
that every deployment is safe.

00:03:27.827 --> 00:03:30.910
Review the attributes, their purpose and their destination.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:37.075
Do not forward a private run to a different service merely because an exporter
supports it.

00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:59.750
Your turn: follow the manual task. Pause for more time.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:04.962
The app can say not configured, invalid configuration, export failed, or export
acknowledged.

00:04:04.962 --> 00:04:06.566
These states are different.

00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:10.575
A connection problem should not become a fake successful trace.

00:04:10.575 --> 00:04:14.985
The exporter uses a bounded single attempt and safe diagnostic categories.

00:04:14.985 --> 00:04:22.603
It must not return raw exception messages, response headers, secret values or a
redirect location that may contain credentials.

00:04:22.603 --> 00:04:30.220
The current reference uses a no-follow redirect policy, rejects redirect responses
and never sends a second credential-bearing request automatically.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.230
A transport acknowledgement proves that the exporter received a response.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:39.442
It does not independently prove that the correct project contains the correct run.

00:04:39.442 --> 00:04:46.658
That distinction is deliberately visible in the application, even when a human has
verified the corresponding trace elsewhere.

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:50.169
The owner view provides the second half of acceptance.

00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:55.164
Find the exact trace and random session that were copied privately from the app.

00:04:55.164 --> 00:04:58.732
Match them before comparing the model, usage and tool structure.

00:04:58.732 --> 00:05:03.726
The fresh recorded Lovable canary was independently correlated with six observations
and two generations.

00:05:03.726 --> 00:05:08.721
The reviewed screenshot omits account controls, project identifiers, private
addresses and exact trace identifiers.

00:05:08.721 --> 00:05:18.711
The provider view can group or order rows differently from an app event list; use
actual timestamps and relationships rather than a screenshot's visual order to infer
sequence.

00:05:18.711 --> 00:05:26.203
Do not pair a screenshot from one app run with a provider trace from another and
call it an exact match.

00:05:26.203 --> 00:05:28.700
Record both sides of the same operation.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.915
The selected historical policy example is labelled with its recording date.

00:05:32.915 --> 00:05:36.830
In the app, the change was blocked with zero model calls.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.610
Its two-span batch was acknowledged.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:44.661
In the independently matched provider view, the tree contains the root run and
authorization, with no generation.

00:05:44.661 --> 00:05:49.643
That absence supports the specific claim that this path did not invoke the model.

00:05:49.643 --> 00:05:53.559
Successful sign-in authorization is not permission to execute the requested change.

00:05:53.559 --> 00:05:57.830
The root status and the no-generation tree explain the safe result together.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:02.101
Keep the date, app result and provider correlation attached to this evidence.

00:06:02.101 --> 00:06:09.575
It is a reproducible policy-path demonstration, not a complete production IAM audit
or proof that every malicious input will be detected.

00:06:09.875 --> 00:06:12.557
Now choose a lower cost native model.

00:06:12.557 --> 00:06:16.005
This recorded canary returned G P T six sol.

00:06:16.005 --> 00:06:23.284
Two calls reported seven hundred sixty one input tokens and one hundred forty two
output, nine hundred three total.

00:06:23.284 --> 00:06:29.414
The app measured three point two one nine seconds; the trace root, three point five
seven.

00:06:29.414 --> 00:06:31.329
Different boundaries explain different clocks.

00:06:31.329 --> 00:06:35.926
Exact trace and random session were matched independently: six observations, two
generations.

00:06:35.926 --> 00:06:40.524
The provider estimated zero point zero zero two nine four two dollars.

00:06:40.524 --> 00:06:45.887
The dated catalogue listed two dollars per million input tokens, ten per million
output.

00:06:45.887 --> 00:06:48.952
This is an estimate, not a Lovable invoice.

00:06:48.952 --> 00:06:52.783
Do not invent missing usage, cache details or billing fees.

00:06:53.083 --> 00:06:57.545
Pause and open a trace that already exists in your own project.

00:06:57.545 --> 00:07:02.378
You do not need to spend more inference credits to learn the basics.

00:07:02.378 --> 00:07:05.352
Identify the root, authorization, generations and tool spans.

00:07:05.352 --> 00:07:06.839
Read the reported usage.

00:07:06.839 --> 00:07:09.813
Check whether prompts and answers are intentionally absent.

00:07:09.813 --> 00:07:12.044
Compare export acknowledgement with independent readback.

00:07:12.044 --> 00:07:18.364
If a trace is missing, begin with configuration presence, destination validation,
export result and the exact identifier.

00:07:18.364 --> 00:07:23.197
Do not run repeated paid canaries just to make the dashboard look busy.

00:07:23.197 --> 00:07:29.146
Preserve the failed attempt, identify the missing receipt, and fix one bounded cause
at a time.

00:07:29.146 --> 00:07:37.325
When you return, we will apply the same product and evidence contract to the
alternative builders, while keeping their current limits explicit.

00:07:37.625 --> 00:08:00.000
Your turn: follow the manual task. Pause for more time.
